UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 168(c) as amended by the Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1993, nonresidential real property placed in service after May 13, 1993 uses a 39-year recovery period, while property placed in service on or before that date retains 31.5 years. The April warehouse qualifies for 31.5 years (~3.17% annually); the June warehouse uses 39 years (~2.56% annually).
Wrong (B): The change was not retroactive; only property placed in service after May 13, 1993 was affected by the longer recovery period.
Wrong (C): The 27.5-year period applies to residential rental property under Section 168(c), not commercial warehouses.
