-- Q538: Individual Taxation: Income [easy/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 465, a taxpayer''s deductible loss is limited to the amount at risk, which includes cash contributed and recourse debt but excludes nonrecourse debt (unless qualified nonrecourse financing on real property). Webber''s at-risk amount is $80,000 (cash only), so only $80,000 of the $150,000 loss is deductible; the remaining $70,000 is suspended.
Wrong (A): At-risk rules apply regardless of AGI level; there is no $250,000 income threshold in Section 465.
Wrong (C): Cash is included in the at-risk amount and nonrecourse debt is excluded, not the reverse.
Wrong (D): Nonrecourse debt is excluded from the at-risk amount; including all borrowings would defeat the rule''s purpose of limiting deductions to economic risk.$EXPL$
