  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 469, passive losses can only offset passive income. Torres has no passive income, so the entire $45,000 loss is suspended and carried forward until passive income arises or the activity is fully disposed of in a taxable transaction. The compartmentalization prevents using tax shelter losses to reduce tax on wages and portfolio income.
Wrong (A): Wages are active income, which is precisely the category that passive losses cannot offset under Section 469.
Wrong (B): Dividends are portfolio income, not passive income; Section 469(e) explicitly excludes portfolio income from the passive category.
